    "thesis": "Venture Global scores 53, a Hold, with strong growth balanced against a weak balance sheet. TTM revenue growth of 100.7% and latest-quarter revenue growth of 47.6% year on year drive a growth score of 75, though growth slowed by 11.3 pp from the previous quarter. Profitability looks healthy at the operating level, with a 53.5% gross margin and a 37.6% operating margin, but the FCF margin is -41.2% as the company keeps spending heavily. That negative cash flow and cash covering only 0.07 of debt leave the balance sheet score at 4. Valuation scores 35: P/S of 2.2x and EV/EBIT of 12.0x are moderate in absolute terms, but the FCF yield is 23.4 pp below the 10-year Treasury yield, and there is no comparison with its own history. The price trend is supportive, with the price 13.6% above its 200-day average.",
